course: dictionary
lesson: 6092
title: Method: a way of doing things
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A method is a planned, careful way of doing something. In maths, when your teacher says «show your method», she wants to see the steps you took, not just the answer.
explain: There can be more than one method for the same sum. You might use column addition, a number line or the grid method, and each one can get the right answer. Context helps here: the words «a different method» tell you that more than one way is possible.
explain: In science, the method is the list of steps you follow in an experiment. It must be clear enough that someone else can repeat it and make it a fair test.
fact: A method is a way of doing something, especially a planned, careful way.
fact: In maths, the method is the steps you use to work out an answer.
fact: In science, the method is the list of steps you follow in an experiment.
fact: «Show your method» means write down the steps, not just the answer.
fact: «Most exoplanets have been found by the transit method»: a star dims slightly when a planet passes in front of it.
exercise: «The Chinese learned to make silk from silkworm cocoons and kept the method secret for centuries.» What does method mean here? | *The way they made silk | The cocoons | The mulberry leaves | The people of Rome
exercise: Mr Patel says, «Show your method.» What should you write down? | A picture of a cat | *Each step you took to get the answer | Your name twice | Only the final answer
exercise: «There are different methods, like column addition and the grid method.» What does this tell you? | Column addition is the only correct method | *The same sum can be solved in more than one way | Maths has no steps at all | The grid method is a kind of sport
test: In science, what is a method? | *The list of steps you follow in an experiment | The answer you get at the end | A kind of equipment | A type of results table
test: Why must a science method be clear? | So the experiment runs faster | The teacher can give you a mark for handwriting | *So someone else can repeat it and make it a fair test | So nobody else can read it
exam: In «a star dims slightly when a planet passes in front of it», what shows how the transit method works? | *The star dims slightly | The planet is made of gas | The planet makes a loud noise | The star gets much bigger
